        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "North Atlantic Deep Water",
            "source_entity_type": "Ocean_Circulation",
            "relation": "OBSERVED_IN_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "North Atlantic",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "On the other hand, the maximum North Atlantic Deep Water (NADW) transport in TED is 16Sv, which is as large as in CTRL (18 Sv). From the view point of global MOC closure, the wind-induced upwelling in the Southern Ocean brings deep water to the ocean surface. A large part of the upwelled water is altered to intermediate and thermocline waters, which are then transported to the North Atlantic in the upper branch of the global MOC and feed the Atlantic MOC.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Deacon cell",
            "source_entity_type": "Ocean_Circulation",
